2026-09-02T00:15:00.000Z note (out-of-band: closed by hand after run 2's gate. Merged with --no-ff. NO freeze re-record is owed and that was checked rather than assumed: git diff 7fd540b..HEAD -- spike/src is empty, because this child touches packages/cli only, and the freeze-SHA half reports clear at the existing anchor. Verified forced on main, the environment row integrate cannot test — and it was RED there at first, which is the whole reason for the row: packages/cli is a new workspace package with dependencies, and an existing checkout has no links for them until pnpm install runs. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` reports "Already up to date" in 180ms and the suite flips green, so the failure looks like a code defect and is not one. CI does a fresh install and never sees it; a developer pulling this merge does. After the install: spike 19/19, workspace 7/7 tasks 0 cached, lint and typecheck 14/14 tasks 0 cached, harness lint 6/6, git-identity sweep green. Six review rounds, six different real subjects, three retries; erratum E-1 is the reusable part, ruling that "Membership is a git question, not a filesystem one" (2026-08-28) does not govern the BYOS scan because that entry argues from what turbo hashes and this guard asks what exists. Q-0091 to Q-0094 may now start against this frame; Q-0095 waits on Q-0096.)
